# 05 - random-LED

## Objective

Make 5 LEDS randomly fade in and out.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 5 LEDs
- 220 Ω resistor
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- random()
- ledcAttach()
- ledcWrite()
- for loops
- variables

## Wiring

|   LED   |               ESP32              |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| Anode   | GPIO 23 (through 220 Ω resistor) |
| Cathode | GND                              |

## Expected Result

The LED turns on for one second and turns off for one second continuously.

## What I Learned

- How to configure an output pin
- How current flows through an LED
- Why a resistor is required
- How the Arduino loop() function works
- How to properly use variables
- How to use delays properly

## Challenges

- Forgot to set the pin as OUTPUT.

## Resources

- ESP32 Documentation
- Arduino Documentation
